    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23251" root="شهو" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْهَى</span></b>  [<i>More,</i> and <i>most, desirable,</i> or <i>pleasant</i>
or <i>delicious</i> or <i>sweet</i>]. One says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ أَشْهَى إِلَىَّ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِنْ كَذَا</span> [<i>It is more desirable,</i> or <i>pleasant</i> &amp;c.,
<i>to me,</i> or <i>in my estimation, than such a thing</i>].
(Msb voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَى</span>.) See also another ex. in a verse
cited voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِلَى</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الو</span>.

